# KrishiMitra AI — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is git-ignored;
# never commit real keys.
#
# When the project is connected through Lovable Cloud, these are injected
# automatically — this file matters for local/self-hosted setups.
#
# Where to find the values: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- server-side
# Used by TanStack Start server functions (src/integrations/supabase/auth-middleware.ts).

# Project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=

# Publishable ("anon") key — safe for browsers, scoped by RLS.
# New-style keys start with `sb_publishable_`; legacy ones end in `anon`.
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# OPTIONAL — secret key that bypasses RLS. Only needed if you use the admin
# client in server code (src/integrations/supabase/client.server.ts).
# New-style keys start with `sb_secret_`; legacy ones end in `service_role`.
# NEVER expose this to the client bundle.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- client-side
# Used by the browser bundle (src/integrations/supabase/client.ts).
# Must be the SAME project as the server vars above.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Optional bookkeeping (not read by app code; informational only).
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=
SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- notes
# 1. The publishable key is NOT a secret — it is safe to ship to browsers.
#    Security comes from Row Level Security policies, which this project
#    enables on every table (see supabase/migrations/).
# 2. The service role key IS a secret. It is intentionally not prefixed with
#    VITE_ so Vite never inlines it into client code.
# 3. To apply database migrations: npx supabase login && npx supabase db push
